      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `tool_choice={\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": ...}}` on the `json_schema` path (`get_json_schema_constraint`, used when the tool-call detector has no structural tag support), the item schema built by `_get_tool_schema` has `properties` and `required` but no `\"type\"`:\n\n```json\n{\"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n \"items\": {\"properties\": {\"name\": {...}, \"parameters\": {...}}, \"required\": [\"name\", \"parameters\"]}}\n```\n\nIn JSON Schema, `properties` and `required` only constrain values that are objects, so `[0]` or `[\"x\"]` is a valid output. xgrammar infers an object from `properties`, which hid this. llguidance follows the spec. The model can then close the array right away (`[`, `0`, `]`, EOS). The parser finds no call and the response comes back with empty `content` and empty `tool_calls`.\n\n`tool_choice=\"required\"` is not affected: it already wraps the branches in `{\"type\": \"object\", \"anyOf\": [...]}`.\n\nCompiling the named schema with llguidance 1.9.1:\n\n| output | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `[0]` | accepted | rejected |\n| `[\"x\"]` | accepted | rejected |\n| `[{\"name\": \"get_time\", \"parameters\": {\"tz\": \"UTC\"}}]` | accepted | accepted |\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `_get_tool_schema` returns `\"type\": \"object\"`. The `required` path, which nests the same dict in a typed `anyOf`, behaves the same as before.\n- Regression test `test_specific_tool_choice_rejects_non_object_items`: `[0]`, `[\"x\"]`, `[None]` and `[[]]` must fail validation and a real call must pass. It fails on main and passes with the fix.\n\nRelated but separate: #40051 touches named `tool_choice` on the legacy structural-tag path, not this `json_schema` item schema.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nConstrained decoding only: the grammar no longer allows call lists whose items are not objects; valid calls are unchanged. Found with `--grammar-backend llguidance` on a model whose tool parser has no structural tag support: the four tokens generated after the reasoning section were `[`, `0`, `]`, EOS.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41606004703](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41606004703)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41606004621](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41606004621)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41606004531](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41606004531)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.age